verdicts.reason:
time_calibrate in lib.rs L394-460:
- runs a latch command from TS_LATCH_CMDS;
- invalidates the cache and reads TimestampValue;
- reads the frequency or increment;
- feeds (dev_ticks, Instant::now()) into TimeSync.

The same code is in the released tag v0.10.0. Frame has ts_dev: Option<u64> and ts_host: Option<SystemTime> at frame.rs L73-75, and Python exposes ts_dev and ts_host at pygenicam frame.rs L145-150.

Caveat: the host side is the monotonic Instant sampled after a GVCP register round trip, so the fit includes network and register-read latency. This is not a PTP host clock.
